ition-colors hover:text-brand-soft">1300 000 082</a></dd></div><div><dt class="text-white/45">Office hours</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-white/75">Monday to Friday, 8:30am to 5pm</dd></div></dl></div></div></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-4 border-b border-white/10 py-8 lg:flex-row lg:items-center lg:gap-10"><p class="shrink-0 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-white/45">Operating across</p><ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-5 gap-y-2 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-white/80"><li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="size-1 bg-brand-soft"></span>Australia</li><li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="size-1 bg-brand-soft"></span>New Zealand</li><li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="size-1 bg-brand-soft"></span>Hong Kong</li><li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="size-1 bg-brand-soft"></span>China</li><li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="size-1 bg-brand-soft"></span>Vietnam</li><li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="size-1 bg-brand-soft"></span>United States</li><li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="size-1 bg-brand-soft"></span>Thailand</li><li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="size-1 bg-brand-soft"></span>Germany</li><li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="size-1 bg-brand-soft"></span>United Kingdom</li></ul></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-2 py-8 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-white/45 sm:flex-row sm:justify-between"><p>© <span>2026</span> <!-- -->Meridian Freight APAC Pty Ltd</p><p>ABN <!-- -->67 262 534 539</p></div></div></footer></div></div></div><script is:inline id="__NEXT_DATA__" type="application/json">{"props":{"pageProps":{"insight":{"id":"31322c61-0215-48c4-815b-d621b1d8e694","slug":"fcl-or-lcl-choosing-the-right-ocean-freight-option","title":"FCL or LCL? Choosing the right ocean freight option","category":"Ocean Freight","excerpt":"Full container or shared space? A practical look at cost, transit time and risk so you can book the right ocean service for every shipment.","published_at":"2026-09-29","body":"\u003cp\u003eEvery ocean shipment starts with the same question: do you book a whole container, or share one with other shippers? Full container load (FCL) and less than container load (LCL) move goods across the same lanes, but they behave very differently on cost, timing and handling.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eHow the two options work\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eWith FCL, the container is yours. It is packed at origin, sealed, and not opened again until it reaches its destination, unless customs or biosecurity officers choose to inspect it. With LCL, your cargo is consolidated with other shipments at a container freight station, travels in a shared box, and is separated again at the destination depot.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eWhen FCL makes sense\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYour cargo fills most of a 20 foot container, roughly 13 to 15 cubic metres or more.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe goods are fragile or high value and you want to keep handling to a minimum.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou need the most predictable transit time, without waiting for consolidation.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch2\u003eWhen LCL makes sense\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou are shipping a few pallets, and a full box would mean paying for empty space.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou want to order smaller quantities more often and hold less stock.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYour timeline can absorb a few extra days for consolidation and deconsolidation at each end.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch2\u003eLook beyond the base rate\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eLCL is priced per cubic metre or per tonne, so it often looks cheaper on paper. Once destination depot charges, handling fees and the extra days in transit are added, the gap can close quickly as volumes grow. Many importers find a tipping point at around half a container, where FCL becomes the better value.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe right answer can change from one shipment to the next. Share your volumes, dimensions and deadlines with our team and we will compare both options side by side before you book.\u003c/p\u003e","cover_image":"/images/meridian/ship-fog.jpg","cover_image_alt":"A container ship emerging from thick fog on calm water"},"related":[{"id":"4bf8b293-4f72-41f6-b760-57ba1cacd285","slug":"what-a-licensed-customs-broker-does-for-importers","title":"What a licensed customs broker actually does for importers","category":"Customs","excerpt":"Classification, valuation, duty and biosecurity all have to line up before goods are released. Here is what a broker handles on your behalf.","published_at":"2026-09-22"},{"id":"c74ac840-3798-4008-882c-478b5bca6df2","slug":"choosing-an-air-freight-service-level","title":"Express, priority or economy: picking an air freight service level","category":"Air Freight","excerpt":"Air freight is not one product. Matching the service level to the urgency of your cargo can save money without putting deadlines at risk.","published_at":"2026-09-15"},{"id":"6eab6307-7ed1-4398-aaf3-e5d3ff81c5e7","slug":"planning-project-cargo-permits-surveys-and-load-engineering","title":"Planning project cargo: permits, surveys and load engineering","category":"Project Cargo","excerpt":"Oversized and heavy lift shipments succeed or fail in the planning stage. These are the steps that keep a complex move on schedule.","published_at":"2026-09-08"}],"news":[{"id":"31322c61-0215-48c4-815b-d621b1d8e694","slug":"fcl-or-lcl-choosing-the-right-ocean-freight-option","title":"FCL or LCL? Choosing the right ocean freight option"},{"id":"4bf8b293-4f72-41f6-b760-57ba1cacd285","slug":"what-a-licensed-customs-broker-does-for-importers","title":"What a licensed customs broker actually does for importers"},{"id":"c74ac840-3798-4008-882c-478b5bca6df2","slug":"choosing-an-air-freight-service-level","title":"Express, priority or economy: picking an air freight service level"}]},"__N_SSG":true},"page":"/insights/[slug]","query":{"slug":"fcl-or-lcl-choosing-the-right-ocean-freight-option"},"buildId":"zlvk7yHoyxO_6eey2QNrr","isFallback":false,"isExperimentalCompile":false,"gsp":true,"scriptLoader":[]}</script><style is:global>[data-modulify-badge]{transition:transform .18s ease,filter .18s ease;will-change:transform}[data-modulify-badge]:hover{transform:translateY(-2px);filter:drop-shadow(0 6px 16px rgba(0,0,0,.16))}[data-modulify-badge]:active{transform:translateY(0)}</style><style is:global>html[data-mdlfy-embedded] [data-modulify-badge]{display:none!important}</style><script is:inline>(function(){try{if(window.top===window.self)return;var a=null;try{a=window.location.ancestorOrigins}catch(e){}var ok=function(o){if(!o)return false;if(o.indexOf("https://")!==0)return false;var h=o.slice(8);var s=h.indexOf("/");if(s!==-1)h=h.slice(0,s);var p=h.indexOf(":");if(p!==-1)h=h.slice(0,p);h=h.toLowerCase();if(h==="modulify.ai")return true;return h.slice(-12)===".modulify.ai"};var owned=false;if(a){if(a.length){owned=true;for(var i=a.length;i--;){if(!ok(a[i]))owned=false}}}else{owned=ok(document.referrer);try{if(owned)window.sessionStorage.setItem("mdlfy-e","1");else if(window.sessionStorage.getItem("mdlfy-e")==="1")owned=true}catch(e){}}if(owned)document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-mdlfy-embedded","1")}catch(e){}})()</script><a href="https://modulify.ai/dashboard/templates/meridian-template" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-modulify-badge="1" style="position:fixed;bottom:16px;right:16px;z-index:2147483647;display:block;text-decoration:none;pointer-events:auto"><img src="data:image/svg+xml;base64," alt="Edit with Modulify" style="height:28px;width:auto;display:block"/></a></body></html>